{"id":"slice4-path-order-landmine","parent":"defc-model","ord":"a0","title":"Slice 4 must pick one path order #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"**Recorded by the slice-3 author (PR #211):** the patcher places an arriving file by assemble's plain string path compare, while the web client's `sortByPath` sorts segment by segment.\n- The two already disagree today — not new unsoundness.\n- But slice 4 (the browser folding delta frames through the same patcher) has to pick one ordering, or the patched browser view will disagree with the assembled one.\n- Filed on the human's overnight draft ruling (\"file roadmap entries for those three\").","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"211","retired":"2026-08-20 verification vs master 44bc6873 — slice 4 landed a third exit: one comparator byPath in @olai/format (paths.ts:42) spent by assemble (set.ts:160), the patcher (patch.ts:291) and the client (web paths.ts:47); orderings pinned by set.test.ts:187,193; and the browser no longer folds through the patcher at all. Nothing left to decide."}}
{"id":"html-unreadable-refused-state","parent":"defc-docs","ord":"a0","title":"An unreadable page says so on the page #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:00-04:00","desc":"#204's deferral 1.\n- Under load-on-read, an unreadable .html (permissions, vanished mid-read) reports only to the server log — the reader sees the page with no body.\n- Telling them needs a `\"refused\"` state on DocumentEntry (a wire change with its own argument) and a face for it.\n- Still quieter than what it replaced, which failed the whole probe and bannered the whole directory.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"204","pr":"#315 merged f5aa92e4 — DocumentEntry gains refused (optional, default false; unreadable-file code only — a frontmatter typo keeps master's blank body + ⚠); bodies.ts and media.ts one story; faces on the page and the DocRef line"}}
{"id":"patch-refile-fifth-spelling","parent":"defc-model","ord":"a1","title":"patch.ts spells re-file-a-reverse-index five times #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:56-04:00","desc":"Counted at PR #237 by the reuse pass.\n\n- **Pattern:** containment, namings, mentions, orderings and blockage each walk the same five steps.\n  - Copy the before-map.\n  - Build arriving.\n  - Gather the keys the edit could have moved from arriving + outgoing.\n  - Per key, take the survivors (filtered by TOUCHED FILE, not by record) plus the arrivals in a promised order.\n  - Drop the key if it ends empty rather than storing an empty list.\n- **#237** added the third of those and designed the extraction rather than skipping it.\n- A generic `refiled<T>` needs the entry `Located` projected back out (the indexes hold different entry shapes), then has to hand back three things: the rewritten map, the keys that VANISHED, and whether a first-namer MOVED.\n- Only `namings` asks for the last two, because only `namedBy` promises key order — two axes behind one contract, with the caller paying for neither unless needed.\n- **Rule invoked:** the repo's existing author rule — a shared fixture is the right move at four occurrences, not three — says the SIXTH index is what should force the extraction.\n- **Why this node exists:** so the sixth becomes the trigger, rather than becoming the sixth silent copy.\n- **Status:** the invariants are re-argued per index today; `patch.test.ts`'s oracle is the only thing holding the copies in step.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"237","pr":"#307 merged 4318cbe8 — refiled<T> over the four true copies; orderings/blockage proven not-the-shape (line evidence in PR + review)"}}
{"id":"follow-one-unit","parent":"defc-nav","ord":"a0","title":"Fold Link and Tree.tsx into useFollow #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T20:32:37-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #284's merge from its Deferrals (the dag gate: a thing left \"for the human\" becomes a roadmap node).\n- #284 gave router.tsx a `useFollow` — the one tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`) — called by PageView's delegated listener and the chat transcript's. Its altitude pass argued that `Link` and `Tree.tsx:396` carry the same two halves (route-off-the-event + open-it) and could be rewired onto it, deleting two exported functions and making the \"one spelling\" claim structural rather than documentary.\n- Not taken there because it is `Link` — every navigation in the app — changed for zero behaviour on a bug-fix PR whose node said do not widen scope. What WAS taken: the two now spell the force bit identically and the Link docstring no longer overclaims.\n- A behaviour-preserving refactor with the whole navigation e2e surface as its net; worth its own small PR when someone is next in router.tsx.","created":"2026-08-20T11:29:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #284 deferral","retired":"2026-08-20 verification vs master 44bc6873, the human's ruling — the Tree.tsx half was never true (Tree.tsx:408 is a decline-guard, not a navigation; unchanged since #246), and #284's own comment at router.tsx:345-351 argues Link's exclusion is deliberate (route already in hand; reading it back off the href is a round trip through a string). The promised delete-two-exports payoff is impossible; closed rather than shrunk."}}
{"id":"names-table-once","parent":"defc-nav","ord":"a1","title":"The names table is built twice per navigation #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T09:17:26-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\" (raised by the efficiency pass).\n- After #287 the names table lives in `names.ts` and holds by value, but `App.tsx` (for the chrome) and each pane (for its own rows) each build one over the focused pane's reading — the same scan twice per frame.\n- The fix is a field on `createReading` and a change to the readings register so the table is derived once beside the reading and read by both — not #287's shape (a `<For>` keying PR).\n- Retired or shrunk by the kolu upstream item (`reactivity-kolu-upstream`) if keyed reconcile lands first, since the per-frame re-derivation is what makes the double scan cost anything.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched","pr":"#314 merged 88470106 — createReading derives the lookup once; pane leaves + palette share it; App.tsx's second site deleted; claims-sweep + run-count probe fence it","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873 — the per-frame half is DISCHARGED by #299 (names.ts:39-46; measured in names.browsertest.ts:167-186: repeated frames and row-moves no longer reach the copy). What survives: both builds re-run per navigation/real rename (names.browsertest.ts:190-197) and a duplicate Map held beside the pane's. Re-scoped to the S tidiness fix: derive once beside the reading (PageView.tsx:74,77 + reading.tsx:294-308 register + App.tsx:248)."}}
{"id":"one-alert-row","parent":"defc-edit","ord":"a0","title":"One markup for the refusal alert row #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","desc":"The palette and the header box hand-roll the `role=\"alert\"` row the filter bar gets from `SaidLine` — one list, one sentence, three markups.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\".\n- #287's `refusals.ts` unified the refusal SENTENCE across the filter bar, the palette and the header search box, and keyed their lines so a refusal is no longer re-announced per keystroke.\n- What is still three-fold is the MARKUP: the filter bar draws its row through `SaidLine`, the palette and the header box hand-roll theirs. Unifying it is a change to what three surfaces draw — its own small PR, with the live-region behaviour (one announcement per new refusal) pinned.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:05-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched","pr":"#310 merged bb10212f — five hand-rolled role=alert rows ride SaidLine; refusals.tsx hoisted to client top"}}
{"id":"shortlist-row-freshness","parent":"defc-search","ord":"a3","title":"Shortlist rows carry their own freshness #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T09:25:21-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from #294's deferrals (strong reason ruled: a design change to surfaces none of that PR's five items name). CORRECTED after grok's review note 3 — the first filing named the doors backwards.\n- #294 gated a stale Enter at the two doors the audit named: `Shortlist.tsx` and `completing.tsx`. Still UNGATED (findings this node absorbs): the composer, palette and header-search takes over the same primitive, and Hypertext's own rewrite-rescroll (#294's \"Seen, not touched\").\n- The deeper shape: rows carrying freshness through `search/Result.tsx` — which all four shortlist doors already draw — or a taker on `createSettled` that cannot be called past a question that has moved. Either fixes the whole class at once instead of per-door gates.\n- The made decision it would subsume: a stale Enter is claimed and spends nothing, silently (dimming was rejected as flicker in a campaign about flicker); a pointer press is never gated.","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:36-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral","pr":"#312 merged e7a5d790 (the three take-doors + pointer ruling pinned) with the Hypertext rewrite-rescroll half closed by #305's landing guard — both halves tracked, nothing buried (grok's finding 2 answered on the PR)"}}
{"id":"router-owns-spent-landing","parent":"defc-nav","ord":"a2","title":"router.landed() — a landing is spent where it is minted #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T07:41:56-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 from #294's deferrals (strong reason ruled: a design change, not a line — Hypertext still reads the slug to BUILD the frame's URL, so it cannot be a hard clear).\n- \"A landing is spent once\" lives in the face today; router.tsx states the contract and enforces nothing. A `router.landed(…)` marking a landing spent (still readable, no longer an act) would put the rule where the value is minted and hand the preview pane (#286's useLanding) the same guard.","created":"2026-08-20T15:17:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #294 deferral","pr":"#305 merged f4a8b7ae — Landing{...spent}, router.landed the one writer; Back 2→1 folded; 3 follow-up questions filed as landing-open-questions"}}
{"id":"team-multi-writer","parent":"defc-git","ord":"a0","title":"Team hosting: several people writing on one branch #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"- The human plans to host olai as a team notebook with coworkers invited.\n- #301 only guarantees the auto loop can't corrupt: it never forces, never retries, never auto-pulls; a refused push stops with git's words on screen.\n- Multi-writer needs real answers: fetch, a merge policy, whose-work-is-whose in the UI, and where rebase-before-push fits (deliberately not automated today — a conflicted rebase is a conversation, not a state the auto loop may enter).","created":"2026-08-20T19:59:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#301"}}
{"id":"filter-highlight-cross-piece","parent":"defc-search","ord":"a0","title":"A phrase across rendered markdown lights neither piece #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:00-04:00","desc":"The surviving half of #240's filter-highlight deferral, closed.\n\n- **#254** (a848677d): a needle inside a code span or link lights; the tag SPLIT stays off under NO_TAGS_IN.\n- **This PR:** a phrase spanning two rendered pieces lights both. One `litBy` over the concatenated visible text of the title's HAST nodes; each node is a window onto that search (the `titleParts`/`runsIn` contract, one level up). Matching still folds the raw source (`foldOf`). Palette and header node-hits run the same `renderTitle` (`links: false`). Completions/Shortlist stay text.\n- **Named leftover, not a child:** a fenced block forced inline in a title — a phrase that crosses that fence into trailing prose is not promised, because the unwrapped fence's visible text is not the title's words, and making it so is a renderer change this lane was forbidden to make. Pin: neither, never one side.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"#240, narrowed by #254","pr":"#316 merged 725ec411 — source offsets threaded through the title render; the old neither-piece pin flipped positive; fence crossing pinned neither-not-half as the honest remainder"}}
{"id":"palette-count-cap","parent":"defc-search","ord":"a1","title":"The palette and header search cap at 8 hits #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T21:25:25-04:00","desc":"Filed at #248's merge (the count-line honesty PR).\n\n- The filtered page's count line now tells all three truths, but the ⌘K palette and the header search box still cap at 8 drawn hits with no denominator — `SearchAnswer.total` is already on the wire and uncounted.\n- Different surface, denominator and hider than the page's count line; also noted in docs/brainstorming/filter-in-place.md.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"#248","pr":"#306 merged 481cbe6e 2026-08-20 — total off the same answer as hits; count.ts sentence + Count.tsx in both doors; picker panels excluded by ruling written into docs/search.md"}}
{"id":"preview-postload-growth","parent":"defc-docs","ord":"a1","title":"A previewed page that grows after loading never gets a taller frame #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T09:52:50-04:00","desc":"#206's deferral 5 — found by three refactor checks and confirmed by a verifier; predates #206, but running JavaScript is exactly what makes drawing late content common, so #206 makes it matter.\n- **Symptom:** a chart drawn from a fetch, a details element the reader opens, a late web font — the frame keeps its pre-growth height.\n- **Converged fix:** instead of rationing height reports per width, accept reports but REJECT THE ECHO — a report within a pixel or two of the frame's own current height is a vh-page feeding its container back; everything else is honest growth.\n- A behavior change wanting its own scenario.","created":"2026-08-16T13:46:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"206","pr":"#313 merged 4581aefb — the node's within-a-pixel rule disproven by measurement; shipped: echo = unchanged gap over the frame + TURNS + one height per painted frame"}}
{"id":"fm-authored-record","parent":"defc-docs","ord":"a2","title":"Frontmatter as the document's own fields #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"- #302 made frontmatter keys searchable properties (prop:/has:). The remaining half: reading them as record fields — a date: drawn on the day page, agenda and calendar; a done: as a mark; edges.\n- Refused in #302 because a frontmatter date that search selects but no page draws would split the grammar — all three date surfaces read Node/Dated.\n- An arc, not a line. Also named in brainstorming/first-class-documents.md, frontmatter.ts, docs/format.md and docs/search.md.\n- Also refused there: tags: values as face tags, and nested/block YAML.","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:41-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"doc-page-props","parent":"defc-docs","ord":"a3","title":"Where should a document page show its own properties? #deferral #needs-brainstorm","desc":"- #302 hides the frontmatter block from the page render; the properties are reachable everywhere else (search rows, read_document, the editor) but the page itself draws them nowhere.\n- Undesigned: a drawer like a node's, a header line, or nothing. A real design pass — documents.feature pins every element of the page.\n- list_documents deliberately reports no props until this is ruled.","created":"2026-08-20T19:53:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#302"}}
{"id":"perf-patch-residue","parent":"defc-model","ord":"a2","title":"The patcher still allocates every record and clones ten indexes per patch #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"- Every patch allocates a flat array of all records (patch.ts:293, load-bearing via Derived.nodes) and copies the byFile map (patch.ts:267).\n- Scope ruled 2026-08-20: fix that medium half. The ten index clones need a delete-capable overlay the docs argue against — that large half stays deferred.\n- The browser side of the original claim is dead (the flip removed the browser fold).","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral (the patcher's flat-list allocation), quantified by the O(n) sweep audit","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873, the human's scope ruling — M half only tonight: the flat [...ordered.values()].flat() (patch.ts:293, load-bearing via Derived.nodes) and new Map(byFile) churn (patch.ts:267). The clone list is now TEN (byDay joined at #278; bench patch.bench.ts:435-436), but the browser side of the claim is dead (fold deleted by the flip) and the ten clones need a delete-capable overlay the docs argue against — that L half stays deferred with these facts."}}
{"id":"perf-faces-broken-walk","parent":"defc-server","ord":"a1","title":"faces/broken walks every key per frame #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T09:06:54-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at #265's merge (rode #263 as deferral 3; #265 numbered it without touching it).\n- faces/broken walks every key per frame; measured +0.1 to +0.3ms of a ~4.5ms frame (spread stated where the numbers live, packages/web/README.md).\n- /simplify in #265 found the cheaper form for whoever picks it up (see the PR's refactor commits for the note).\n- Deliberately untouched by #265 — not one of its four items.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral 3, requantified by #265","pr":"#311 merged 50baf9b1 — one walk for faces+broken+paths; heads-fold deferred godly, filed as directory-heads-fold","verified":"2026-08-20 vs 44bc6873 — APPLIES verbatim (directory.ts:107-140 names this node in its own comment; faces has no equals, broken pays the same walk; facesOf still flatMaps per file). CAVEAT: the cited numbers' bench (outlines.bench.ts) was deleted by #279 and packages/web/README.md no longer carries them — evidence must be a run-count browsertest probe, not a bench. Cheaper form from #265 still exactly applicable: one merged walk producing both."}}
{"id":"e2e-underload-full-census","parent":"defc-tests","ord":"a0","title":"e2e: run the full-suite flake census at scale #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T08:02:42-04:00","desc":"Run the full-suite flake census at scale — `underload.sh RUNS=20 BUSY=48` / `SUITES=5` — after the scratch-sharing change.\n\nFiled 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (opencode: verification work not yet run — a deferral, not a finding).\n- #281 ran underload.sh on the two converted files only (RUNS=3: 3 runs, 0 drops). The full-suite run at the census's own settings takes hours and the spawn saving was 16 of 502, so the lane did not pay for it.\n- Worth running once, unattended, to learn whether the port/lock failure class moved at all and to re-baseline the census after the ~150-scenario cut and the sharing change. Output is a number in the README's census paragraph, not a code change.","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:24-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral","pr":"#309 merged c72e4be7 — census re-baselined on kolu-ci-6 at 399cf308; numbers in packages/tests/README.md"}}
{"id":"filter-ask-carries-revision","parent":"defc-search","ord":"a2","title":"A filtered page re-searches the whole vault every frame #needs-brainstorm #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"- Measured in #290 on a 90k-node vault: one bulk gesture costs nine whole-vault search calls, one per frame. No client-side coalescing window can honestly reduce it (built both ways, measured 9→8, deleted).\n- The fix is on the server side: either the ask carries the page's revision so an unmoved set is answered from what was already computed, or the narrowing moves to the server with the reading.\n- Wants a short design note first: which of the two, the wire shape, and what the reconnect re-ask becomes.","see":["reactivity-kolu-upstream"],"created":"2026-08-20T14:01:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #290 deferral"}}
{"id":"changed-frame-tax-upstream","parent":"defc-upstream","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: changed()'s per-frame cost belongs in kolu #deferral #kolu-upstream","desc":"- Four kolu follow-ups from #299 (the reactivity finale), each ruled deferrable by its review:\n  - Registering on changed()/arrayKey drops the tracker into whole-frame comparisons; the cheaper spine-walk shape belongs upstream.\n  - The keyed merge leaves the tracker holding a second full copy of every frame.\n  - The per-member schema guard answers a question every kolu app has; kolu's own guard doesn't check it.\n  - Batched deltas delivery can't honour a key, so key declarations buy nothing there.\n- Kolu-repo work — needs the human's ratification before filing.","created":"2026-08-20T18:14:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#299"}}
{"id":"preview-atx-regex","parent":"defc-docs","ord":"a4","title":"preview.ts still carries the quadratic heading-trim regex #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"- preview.ts:55 has /\\s+#+$/ — the second half of the ATX pair slug.ts documents as quadratic.\n- Low severity: the operand is one preview line of your own note. Filed so the next redos pass starts from a pointer instead of a hunt.","created":"2026-08-20T22:20:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#304"}}
{"id":"landing-open-questions","parent":"defc-nav","ord":"a3","title":"Landing: is one history entry per write on a previewed page livable? #deferral #needs-brainstorm","doing":true,"desc":"- #319 closed three of the four landing questions with one rule: a landing's geometry may only correct an act still in flight, and flight ends when the reader moves the frame or the 2s window runs out; each pane lands its own.\n- What remains: a revision bump on a previewed .html still costs ONE history entry (down from three).\n- Getting to zero means loading a second iframe behind the first and swapping on load — doubles the frame's state machine and changes what's on screen during the fetch. Ruled expensive at #319.\n- Wants the human's ruling: live with one entry per write, or pay for the doubled machine.","created":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:04:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"#305","pr":"#319 merged 1d640926 closed Q2/Q3/Q4; Q1 remains"}}
{"id":"said-home-and-nudge","parent":"defc-edit","ord":"a1","title":"SaidLine's home, and whether the editor's nudge speaks #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T12:26:16-04:00","desc":"Two leftovers from #310: (1) the editor's refusal carries data-kind and its nudge sibling has no role/aria-live — routing them through SaidLine would CHANGE what a screen reader is told (role=status aria-live=polite), a behavior ruling, plus a data-kind passthrough beside data-tone. (2) SaidLine still lives under edit/ with fourteen importers across eleven directories; moving it drags the Said type out of edit/undoing.ts — a where-does-the-two-mood-type-belong design question, not a file move.","created":"2026-08-21T07:41:57-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"#310","pr":"#318 merged 6b077271 — SaidLine at the client top with the Said type; data-kind beside data-tone; the nudge speaks (role=status polite, red-first); a third hand-rolled hold-out folded; the only-SaidLine-reads-a-mood sweep"}}
{"id":"directory-heads-fold","parent":"defc-server","ord":"a0","title":"The directory rides heads' collection fold #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T12:00:18-04:00","desc":"#311 halved the constant (one walk per frame, paths carried out of it) but a frame naming one file still reads every file, sorts on membership moves, and mints a fresh paths array. heads is served with batched deltas — the delivery knows which keys moved — and @kolu/surface hands that over as a collection fold, the same socket chat/order.ts retired the transcript's per-frame sort on. Ruled godly at #311 (twice-reviewed): the fold inherits invalidated-until-next-snapshot semantics (a state this directory has no answer for; the manifest cell's three-state argument would have to absorb it) and needs an accumulator maintaining path order incrementally (chat/order.ts's ordered() over a comparator instead of a number); it also widens the HeadEntries seam (a fold is registered, not read). walkOf's docstring and packages/web/README.md's \"What is still whole-set\" both point here.","created":"2026-08-21T09:06:54-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:55-04:00","custom":{"from":"#311","pr":"#317 merged 99c3c26f — SERVED_FILES rides the collection fold; a frame costs the frame; absent state absorbed by the manifest"}}
